# The same system said a different way. One row per relabelling: what it rewrites, the sentence
# in the schema that says a rule must not notice, and whether the model claims the verdicts hold
# still.
#
# A covering word is a claim about what the rules cannot see
#   Without this roster nothing here would test it. `HolderKind` says "unserved" and not
#   "refused", and argues the choice: both of the other two name an actor, a card that errors a
#   request did refuse it, a caller who waits past their patience was refused by nobody. Then
#   the load-bearing sentence: both land in the same two holders, so the word covering them must
#   not decide which happened. That is a falsifiable statement about every rule in checks/, and
#   a statement like that asserted in prose and checked by nothing is the condition the whole
#   checks/ tree exists to end.
#
# The test is a rewrite, not a new filing
#   Say the shortfall twice, once as a refusal and once as a decay, holding the demand, the
#   nameplate, the remainder, the fit, the holders and every magnitude fixed. If a rule returns
#   a different verdict on the two, the rule decided which happened, and the covering word has a
#   counter-example.
#
# The third row is the defeater
#   It is not optional. Two relabellings expected to hold still are two ways of learning
#   nothing, because a harness that compares a relation to itself reports `steady` for every
#   input including a broken one. `unserved_as_absorbed` crosses a line the rules do read, so it
#   must move; the day it does not, the diff is wrong and the other two rows are worth nothing.
#   Same argument as the three deliberate defects the validator was made to reject before any
#   pass was believed.
#
# `expected` is the gate, `swaps` is the parameter
#   The rewrites live in assets/sql/invariance.sql as statements, because a perturbation is not
#   a relation; what each one is for is here, where it can be read without running anything.
-- pm:HolderKind, the "unserved" annotation; pm:Layer/pm:timeSlack, "the holder does not get to refuse".
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('refusal_as_decay',
   'capacity slack <-> time slack, on a layer whose shortfall nobody could serve',
   'the same demand went without because the supply had no room to run into, or because it did not survive the wait',
   'steady'),
  ('experienced_or_not',
   'customer <-> unrealised, on every layer, including the ones naming both',
   'demand that was there and got degraded, or demand that never became anybody''s experience',
   'steady'),
  ('unserved_as_absorbed',
   'customer -> people, where a layer has no people holder already',
   'the defeater: this one crosses unserved into absorbed, which the rules read on purpose',
   'moves')
) AS t(slug, swaps, tests, expected)
